@@ -5,4 +5,13 @@ a title, a priority and a few tags, tick them off when they are done, and look a
 urgent first. This package holds the list itself, in TypeScript; the app's screens use its public API
 from `src/index.ts`.
 
+## Input rules
+
+Adding, renaming and tagging a task check what was typed, and refuse it with an error that says what is
+wrong. A refused change leaves the list as it was.
+
+- A title cannot be empty or only spaces, and cannot be longer than 120 characters. Surrounding spaces do not count.
+- A priority is `low`, `normal` or `high`; a task without one is `normal`.
+- A tag cannot be empty and cannot contain a space (any whitespace counts as a space).
+
 Run its tests with `npm test`.
